Z||000008||grinthock||05-01-2001||09:24 AM||||Damaging a Fiero is against the law, not sure what section, but I beleive it reads.<P><BR>a)  Any person or persons found damaging a Pontiac Fiero, either intentionally, willfully or through malice, disregard or negligence is guilty of an Indictible Offense under the Criminal Code of Canada and is subject to a minimum $5000 fine and 90 days in jail to life, to be determined by the Criminal Court General division.<P>b)  Any person or persons found endangering a Pontiac Fiero is guilty of a Summary offense under the Criminal Code of Canada and is subject to a minumum $2500 fine and 30 days in custody.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Cheever2||05-01-2001||10:18 AM||||Wow, Eric, looks like some peeps told you a thing or two.  I won't do that, since I wasn't there & didn't see it.  Same as I won't pass judgement on street racers or people who don't believe in aspartame poisoning.<P>I was recently passed on the highway by an elderly couple in a gold coupe, and <B>they <I>waved</I></B>, even without waiting for me to wave first!  I was stunned.  Very rare for that to happen.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000010||ChadMan||05-01-2001||10:48 AM||||I think some of you guys are being a little hard on Eric.  It doesn't sound like he did anything too crazy...just followed too close on an offramp.  I see people doing way worse stuff than that every day on my way to work.<P>I passed a really nice, clean, red 2M4 last fall on 315 South...he was going about 60 in the middle lane and I was going 75 in the fast line.  I slowed down, honked, waved, and smiled...he stared straight ahead, so I downshifted and drove away.  Wonder if it was the same guy?||||reg||11
