Z||000012||Eric||05-01-2001||11:35 AM||||Wow!?  I can't believe you think I would put myself, my Fiero, or another driver and Fiero at risk.  I'm just proud of my car, and I thought he may feel the same way about his car, so I made an effort to wave at him.  I know there are a lot of other people who drive fast on on-ramps too.  This guy was just going really slow so there was a  speed differential at the exit (nothing my brakes couldn't handle  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<P>Chadman, the car was nice and clean.  The driver was fifty something with gray hair and no sense of humor, kinda like the rest of you!||||reg||1
Z||000013||Mach10||05-01-2001||12:13 PM||||If'n you'd tried that up here, you'd have hit a pothole, broke a spindle, bounced off an igloo, and landed in a hockey rink, about to be torn apart by irate players, and sea-gull sized mosquitoes.<P>I say we charge this guy under the "Shinanigans Act" of 1999. I've got my broomstick handy... Shinanigans! I declare Shinanigans! (thud-thud-thud-thwack)<P>Well, "limit of traction" kinda tells me "too fast" but hey, I do that around corners here in my Mazda. Just NEVER with anyone else within 100 meters of me. No-one got hurt, and you had some fun... 'S all good. <P>Just don't expect any sympathy if you end up with your ass in the air in a ditch...<P>btw... Did I miss any stereotypic canadian road hazards?||||reg||10
